    {
      "slug": "the-vision-of-saint-bernard-fra-bartolomeo",
      "title": "The Vision of Saint Bernard (Fra Bartolomeo)",
      "year": 1504,
      "imageUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c6/Fra_bartolomeo_02_Vision_of_St_Bernard_with_Sts_Benedict_and_John_the_Evangelist.jpg",
      "imageWidth": 1065,
      "imageHeight": 1027,
      "story": "The Vision of Saint Bernard is an oil painting on panel by the Italian artist Fra Bartolomeo, datable to 1504–1507. It is held in the Uffizi, in Florence.",
      "facts": [
        "The miraculous tale appears normalized in everyday life, emphasized only by the grandeur of the Michelangelo-inspired forms.",
        "In 1504, four years after Fra Bartolomeo had taken his vows, the prior of the Convent of San Marco, where he lived, suggested him to return to painting, which he had not done since taking the Dominican habit."
      ],
      "wikipediaUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Vision_of_Saint_Bernard_(Fra_Bartolomeo)",
